From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 07:48:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: something modesets

`DrmScreen` answered `CreateScreen()`, and nothing ever gave it a display: the
only caller of `OnDisplaysChanged` was `InitScreen`, passing the empty list, so
every run reported the displayless fallback and no CRTC was ever lit.

On ChromeOS the thing that would is `DisplayConfigurator`, in
`//ui/display/manager` behind `assert(is_chromeos)`. Only that CALLER is
ChromeOS-only. Every seam it drives is ungated and already implemented by
`DrmNativeDisplayDelegate` -- `Initialize`, `GetDisplays`, `Configure`, and the
two-method `NativeDisplayObserver` that reports a hotplug. So this is a caller
and not a port, and it takes none of `DisplayChangeObserver`'s 478 lines, whose
output is `ManagedDisplayInfo`: ChromeOS product surface nothing here reads.

`ModesetParamsFromSnapshots` is a free function so that the arithmetic has a
test. Everything around it is a delegate, two asynchronous callbacks and a
thread, and that is what the browser exercises rather than a unit test.

IT SKIPS A CONNECTOR WITH NO NATIVE MODE, which is the opposite of what
`DisplaysFromSnapshots` does with the same input. The asymmetry is the point: a
display list must answer for every connector because a window has to land
somewhere, and a modeset must not invent a mode the hardware never advertised.
Asking a CRTC for a mode that was never reported is how a screen goes black
rather than wrong.

The screen is fed before the modeset is attempted, from the same reading, so
the display list the browser sees and the CRTCs that get lit cannot disagree --
and a window still has somewhere to land if the modeset is refused.

The snapshot vector is `raw_ptr<..., VectorExperimental>` throughout now.
`GetDisplaysCallback` uses that type and `DrmScreen` used the default traits,
which are different types and do not convert; upstream's own
`DrmDisplayHostManager` uses the same spelling this now does.
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn              |  3 +++
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc | 20 ++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
index ffee3908..1d789a5c 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
@@ -120,6 +120,8 @@ source_set("gbm") {
     "host/drm_window_host.cc",
     "host/drm_window_host.h",
     "host/drm_window_host_manager.cc",
+    "domicile/drm_modeset.cc",
+    "domicile/drm_modeset.h",
     "domicile/drm_screen.cc",
     "domicile/drm_screen.h",
     "host/drm_window_host_manager.h",
@@ -232,6 +234,7 @@ source_set("gbm_unittests") {
     "gpu/mock_drm_modifiers_filter.cc",
     "gpu/mock_drm_modifiers_filter.h",
     "gpu/proxy_helpers_unittest.cc",
+    "domicile/drm_modeset_unittest.cc",
     "domicile/drm_screen_unittest.cc",
   ]
 
diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc
index 662ee090..3fd2c99b 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_display_host_manager.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_native_display_delegate.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h"
+#include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/domicile/drm_modeset.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/domicile/drm_screen.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host_manager.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/host_drm_device.h"
@@ -100,11 +101,15 @@ class OzonePlatformDrm : public OzonePlatform {
     return std::make_unique<DrmScreen>(window_manager_.get());
   }
   void InitScreen(PlatformScreen* screen) override {
-    // The display list arrives from DrmNativeDisplayDelegate, which the
-    // modeset driver owns; until it has run there are no snapshots, and
-    // DrmScreen answers with the displayless fallback its header describes
-    // rather than with nothing.
+    // Start the modeset driver here, and not earlier, because here is where
+    // the screen it feeds first exists. It asks DrmNativeDisplayDelegate for
+    // the display list and lights what comes back; until that answer arrives
+    // DrmScreen reports the displayless fallback its header describes, which
+    // is why this seeds it rather than leaving the list empty.
     static_cast<DrmScreen*>(screen)->OnDisplaysChanged({});
+    modeset_ = std::make_unique<DrmModeset>(CreateNativeDisplayDelegate(),
+                                            static_cast<DrmScreen*>(screen));
+    modeset_->Start();
   }
 
   GpuPlatformSupportHost* GetGpuPlatformSupportHost() override {
@@ -383,6 +388,13 @@ class OzonePlatformDrm : public OzonePlatform {
   std::unique_ptr<DrmCursor> cursor_;
   std::unique_ptr<EventFactoryEvdev> event_factory_ozone_;
   std::unique_ptr<DrmDisplayHostManager> display_manager_;
+
+  // Domicile's engine fork: what drives NativeDisplayDelegate so that
+  // something actually modesets. On ChromeOS that caller is
+  // DisplayConfigurator, which lives behind assert(is_chromeos). Declared
+  // after display_manager_ so it is destroyed before the manager whose
+  // delegate it holds.
+  std::unique_ptr<DrmModeset> modeset_;
   PlatformRuntimeProperties host_properties_;
 
   base::WeakPtrFactory<OzonePlatformDrm> weak_factory_{this};
